    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "Continue the pattern $6^{3}=216$, $6^{2}=36$, $6^{1}=6$ to find $6^{0}$.\nExplain why the answer is not $0$.",
        "solution_text": "Each step down in the index divides by the base $6$.\n$6^{2}=216\\div6=36$\n$6^{1}=36\\div6=6$\n$6^{0}=6\\div6=1$.\nThe next step divides $6$ by $6$; it does not make the value zero."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Use $8^{3}\\div8^{3}$ to establish the value of $8^{0}$.",
        "solution_text": "The division law subtracts the indices:\n$8^{3}\\div8^{3}=8^{3-3}=8^{0}$.\nAlso, $8^{3}=512$ and $512\\div512=1$.\nBoth expressions describe the same division, so $8^{0}=1$.\nThe base is nonzero, so dividing by this power is allowed."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Evaluate.\n(a) $(-7)^{0}$\n(b) $-7^{0}$\n(c) $\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^{0}$",
        "solution_text": "(a) The whole bracket is the nonzero base, so $(-7)^{0}=1$.\n(b) The index is attached only to $7$. The minus sign stays outside.\n$-7^{0}=-\\left(7^{0}\\right)=-1$.\n(c) The base $\\frac{1}{5}$ is nonzero, so $\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^{0}=1$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "(a) Evaluate $0^{4}$.\n(b) Explain why the zero-index rule cannot be used to give $0^{0}$ a value.",
        "solution_text": "(a) $0^{4}=0\\times0\\times0\\times0=0$.\nThis is a zero base with a positive index.\n(b) The rule $a^{0}=1$ requires a nonzero base, so it does not apply to $0^{0}$.\nThe rule $0^{n}=0$ requires a positive whole-number index, so it does not apply either.\nThe division argument would require $0\\div0$, which is not allowed. In this work, $0^{0}$ is left undefined."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "(a) Evaluate $13\\times6^{0}+5^{0}$.\n(b) Arrange $-8^{0}$, $0^{8}$ and $(-8)^{0}$ in ascending order.",
        "solution_text": "(a) Evaluate each zero power before the remaining operations.\n$13\\times6^{0}+5^{0}=13\\times1+1=14$.\n(b) $-8^{0}=-1$, $0^{8}=0$ and $(-8)^{0}=1$.\nSince $-1<0<1$, the ascending order is $-8^{0},\\ 0^{8},\\ (-8)^{0}$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Evaluate.\n(a) $\\left(23^{8}\\right)^{0}$\n(b) $\\left(4^{0}\\right)^{6}-(-8)^{0}+0^{2}$",
        "solution_text": "(a) $23^{8}$ is nonzero, so $\\left(23^{8}\\right)^{0}=1$. There is no need to work out $23^{8}$.\n(b) First replace the zero powers of nonzero bases by $1$.\n$\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}\\left(4^{0}\\right)^{6}-(-8)^{0}+0^{2}\\\\&=1^{6}-1+0\\\\&=1-1+0\\\\&=0\\end{aligned}$"
      }
    ],
